# Offline-first default CI path: build and run the primary C++ (hxcpp) test
# suite with `-D offline`, which force-skips every internet-dependent case.
# Loopback cases (framing, flush, EOF, buffer caps, manual poll, non-routable
# timeout) still run; mTLS cases pass or SKIP cleanly when openssl is absent
# or misbehaves. This is the documented no-network CI command.
#
#   haxe tests_offline.hxml
#
# Equivalent to: haxe -D offline tests_cpp.hxml
# Requires: haxe, the utest and hxcpp haxelibs, and a working C++ toolchain.
-debug
-D offline
-lib utest
-lib hxcpp
-cp src
-cp tests
-main hxSockets.tests.HaxeSocketTests
-cpp tests/cpp
-cmd echo "Running C++ tests (offline)..." && tests/cpp/HaxeSocketTests-debug
